Z||000000||AL||09-10-1999||01:25 AM||||<BR>like to ask, does the fan motor work on any of your cars? plus where is the horns at?i have 86 gt that i just bought and i can't find the horns. also does anyone have the scamatics of this car? if so please send it to me.by the way i mean the fan motor in the rear.||||reg||
Z||000001||TOM||09-10-1999||01:50 AM||||The coil and alternator cooling fan only come on when the a/c is on or the over temp light light comes on. I do have a schematic but in paper form not digital. I will answer any questions I can.||||reg||
Z||000002||ChadMan||09-10-1999||08:59 AM||||Mine works!  It's pretty quiet, too.  I didn't realize it was on until I stuck my hand in front of the tube and felt the airflow.||||reg||
Z||000003||theogre||09-10-1999||09:37 AM||||the horns are under the car. front right side below the radiator.||||reg||
Z||000004||AL||09-10-1999||11:30 PM||||yea but are you talkin about the motor in the rear?i thought that motor came on whenyou turned on car?so about the scamatics? is it possible for you to copy it and send it to me in the real mail?if so i can give you my address.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||09-11-1999||03:22 AM||||That is funny, I had a friend ask me what in the heck those tubes were.  I had no clue at the time, and shrugged it off as some wacky GM design.  While working on the sequential turn signals (another post on this board)I stumbled upon the motor and figured it out.  That just seems like a really neat idea(too bad it isnt a blower into the intake manifold too).<P>The wiring schematics are in the chilton repair manual.  You can likely find one in a public library, or spring the 15 or so bucks and get one at a store.||||reg||12
