Z||000008||AL||09-12-1999||04:38 PM||||well my radiator fan came on but not the rear, guess it screwed up, time to buy another one?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Linx||09-12-1999||11:22 PM||||There's a second fan for shooting air thru those mysterious tubes in the engine compartment?  I'd long ago discovered their use, but I've always thought it was air channeled from the pressurized (when fan on) underhood radiator compartment.  Where the heck is this second fan?  (and I thought I knew this car's innards like the back o' my hand)||||reg||4
Z||000010||ChadMan||09-13-1999||09:07 AM||||When you're standing behind the car and raise the deck lid, notice the "hump" at the upper right corner of the trunk (no jokes please!).  If you pull back the carpet, you'll see the fan.  It sucks fresh air from under the car and blows it through those tubes onto the coil and alternator.<P>Mine only comes on when the radiator fan is running.  Try turning on your A/C - that should turn on the radiator fan and trunk-mounted auxiliary fan.||||reg||1
Z||000011||AL||09-14-1999||12:43 AM||||i will try turning on  the air, to see if it does come on.i'm not that woried about it, because i just finished putting in new heads in it, and it doesn't get hot at all, but, i'm like alot of you, i like for everything to work right. also when i brake, i've noticed that the lights inside the dash and outside, they turn on but as soon as i release the brake they turn off. the light switch wrks when i turn the lights on but when i brake they come on as well, do all fieros do this? especially the gt's?||||reg||1
Z||000012||RFMike||09-14-1999||10:37 PM||||Not good,Al.  The dash lights should not come on with the brake lights.  Could be a short between the dash light circuit and the brake light circuit.||||reg||1
